WEBVTT

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:30.540
And I've developed some guidelines

00:05:30.564 --> 00:05:32.728
about how to avoid stepping on them.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.786
Let's start with one kind of authenticity:

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:38.886
emotional vulnerability,

00:05:38.910 --> 00:05:41.186
letting people see your real feelings,

00:05:41.210 --> 00:05:43.462
like Mohamed with those metal traders.

00:05:44.097 --> 00:05:45.576
We all get nervous.

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:48.816
Sometimes we're encouraged
to fake it till we make it.

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:51.296
But Mohamed chose to be real

00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:53.146
and sprinkled in some humor, too.

00:05:53.170 --> 00:05:55.474
ME: I said, "I've been told
that last year

00:05:55.498 --> 00:05:59.373
you took to the bread rolls
that you have in front of you

00:05:59.397 --> 00:06:01.194
and threw it at the speaker.